# sepolicy.rule -- optional module SELinux policy additions.
#
# Add only narrowly scoped, reviewed rules justified by an observed AVC denial.
# Use the SELinux Repair workflow to identify the acting domain, a concrete
# target label, class, and permission before adding anything here.
#
# Never use permissive domains, broad generic labels, dontaudit to hide a
# denial, or raw audit2allow output as a final rule.
#
# Example shape only; replace every placeholder after evidence-based review:
# allow <module_domain> <specific_target_type>:file { read open getattr };